# Shell scripts must keep LF endings no matter how they are checked out.
#
# The Windows CI job runs .github/scripts/*.sh through Git Bash's `sh`, and the
# linux/macos jobs run them through bash. A CRLF shebang line ("bash\r") fails
# with "bad interpreter", and a stray CR inside a parsed value is a silent
# wrong-answer bug rather than a loud one. Declaring it here keeps the scripts
# byte-identical across the three runners instead of relying on each developer's
# core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The workflow and scripts are YAML/shell; keep them LF too so diffs stay
# readable and nothing downstream has to cope with mixed endings.
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
